{#- Article 06: how the PQXDH session secret is built. Alice's keys on the
    left, Bob's prekey bundle on the right, the four X25519 exchanges and the
    ML-KEM-768 encapsulation in the middle (DH4 dashed: absent from today's
    cards). Below, the key material as a segmented bar, then HKDF-SHA256 and
    its two outputs. Classical parts in the neutral line colour, the
    post-quantum part in the accent. No transport colour: nothing travels
    here. ids are prefixed with the diagram name. No blank line (Markdown). -#}
{%- set t = {
  en: {
    title: "How Barking builds a session secret from X25519 and ML-KEM-768",
    desc: "On the left, Alice's keys: identity key IK_A and ephemeral key EK_A. On the right, Bob's prekey bundle: identity key IK_B, signed prekey SPK_B and an ML-KEM-768 key. In the middle, four X25519 exchanges: DH1 = IK_A × SPK_B, DH2 = EK_A × IK_B, DH3 = EK_A × SPK_B, and DH4 = EK_A × a one-time prekey, optional and absent from current cards. Then an ML-KEM-768 encapsulation to Bob's key. Below, the key material: 32 bytes of 0xFF, DH1, DH2, DH3, optional DH4, then the ML-KEM secret, 192 bytes at most. It goes into HKDF-SHA256, which outputs the session key and the mailbox secret. The exchanges are classical; the ML-KEM secret is post-quantum.",
    alice: "Alice", bob: "Bob · prekey bundle",
    ik: "identity", ek: "ephemeral", spk: "signed prekey", pq: "ML-KEM-768 key",
    optional: "optional, absent from current cards", kem: "ML-KEM-768 encapsulation",
    km: "key material · 192 bytes at most",
    classical: "classical (X25519)", post: "post-quantum (ML-KEM-768)",
    sk: "session key", mb: "mailbox secret"
  },
  fr: {
    title: "Comment Barking construit un secret de session à partir de X25519 et ML-KEM-768",
    desc: "À gauche, les clés d’Alice : clé d’identité IK_A et clé éphémère EK_A. À droite, le paquet de préclés de Bob : clé d’identité IK_B, préclé signée SPK_B et clé ML-KEM-768. Au centre, quatre échanges X25519 : DH1 = IK_A × SPK_B, DH2 = EK_A × IK_B, DH3 = EK_A × SPK_B, et DH4 = EK_A × une clé à usage unique, optionnel et absent des cartes actuelles. Puis une encapsulation ML-KEM-768 vers la clé de Bob. En bas, le matériel de clé : 32 octets 0xFF, DH1, DH2, DH3, DH4 éventuel, puis le secret ML-KEM, 192 octets au plus. Il entre dans HKDF-SHA256, qui en sort la clé de session et le secret des boîtes. Les échanges sont classiques ; le secret ML-KEM est post-quantique.",
    alice: "Alice", bob: "Bob · paquet de préclés",
    ik: "identité", ek: "éphémère", spk: "préclé signée", pq: "clé ML-KEM-768",
    optional: "optionnel, absent des cartes actuelles", kem: "encapsulation ML-KEM-768",
    km: "matériel de clé · 192 octets au plus",
    classical: "classique (X25519)", post: "post-quantique (ML-KEM-768)",
    sk: "clé de session", mb: "secret des boîtes"
  }
}[lang] -%}
